      "id": "background",
      "navLabel": "Background",
      "title": "Historical Background",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "context",
          "heading": "The City of Colossae",
          "body": [
            {
              "p": "<strong>Location:</strong> Colossae was located in the Lycus River valley in ancient Phrygia (modern-day Turkey), about 100 miles east of Ephesus. It sat alongside two other cities: Laodicea and Hierapolis."
            },
            {
              "p": "<strong>Economic Status:</strong> Once a prosperous city on major trade routes, by Paul's time Colossae had declined in importance, overshadowed by nearby Laodicea. The city was known for its wool industry and distinctive dark red/purple dye called \"colossinus.\""
            },
            {
              "p": "<strong>Religious Climate:</strong> The city was a melting pot of religions - Greek polytheism, Roman imperial cult, Jewish communities, and various mystery religions and philosophical schools converged here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "themes",
          "heading": "Paul's Connection to Colossae",
          "body": [
            {
              "p": "<strong>Likely never visited personally</strong> (Col. 2:1 suggests this), but had strong connections through:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "<strong>Epaphras</strong> - Probably founded the church there (Col. 1:7, 4:12)",
                "<strong>Philemon</strong> - Church likely met in his house",
                "<strong>Onesimus</strong> - The runaway slave was from Colossae (Col. 4:9)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "warning",
          "heading": "The Colossian Heresy",
          "body": [
            {
              "p": "Paul wrote to combat a dangerous syncretistic teaching that combined several elements:"
            },
            {
              "h4": "Mystical Elements:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "Worship of angels as intermediaries (Col. 2:18)",
                "Claims of special visions and revelations",
                "Secret knowledge (gnosis) required for spiritual maturity"
              ]
            },
            {
              "h4": "Jewish Legalistic Elements:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "Observance of festivals, new moons, Sabbaths (Col. 2:16)",
                "Dietary restrictions and food laws",
                "Circumcision requirements"
              ]
            },
            {
              "h4": "Ascetic Practices:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "\"Do not handle, taste, or touch\" (Col. 2:21)",
                "Harsh treatment of the body (Col. 2:23)",
                "Self-imposed worship and humility"
              ]
            },
            {
              "h4": "Philosophical Components:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "Greek philosophical traditions",
                "Human wisdom and traditions (Col. 2:8)",
                "Elementary principles of the world"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "application",
          "heading": "Modern Parallels",
          "body": [
            {
              "p": "Today's believers face similar challenges:"
            },
            {
              "ul": [
                "<strong>New Age Spirituality:</strong> Angels, crystals, channeling",
                "<strong>Prosperity Gospel:</strong> Adding works to faith for blessing",
                "<strong>Legalism:</strong> Rules-based Christianity",
                "<strong>Secular Philosophy:</strong> Humanism, relativism, scientism",
                "<strong>Religious Syncretism:</strong> Mixing Christianity with other beliefs"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "reflection",
          "heading": "Reflection Questions",
          "questions": [
            {
              "audience": "Personal",
              "text": "What modern teachings or philosophies do you find most appealing or challenging to your faith?"
            },
            {
              "audience": "Group Discussion",
              "text": "How can we identify and guard against teachings that add to or subtract from the gospel?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "notes",
          "heading": "Your Notes on Background",
          "id": "notes-background-1",
          "placeholder": "Write your observations, questions, or insights about the historical background..."
        },
